h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitivity to the background and conditions of victims and the use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy; and
l. fulfillment of women's rights.

Article 63
(1) Facilitation of the juvenile justice system includes criminal and civil justice.
(2) Facilitation of the criminal justice system as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. provision of companions or child volunteers during examination by investigators;
b. provision of legal and psychological assistance services;
c. involving members/officers/investigators of the local police in efforts to prevent criminal acts committed by children, children as victims, and children as witnesses;
d. realizing restorative justice processes for children in conflict with the law; and
e. rehabilitation and social reintegration services;
(3) Fulfillment of children's rights in the civil justice system as referred to in paragraph (1) includes the provision and delivery of consultation and legal assistance services during the judicial process.
(4) In facilitating the juvenile justice system as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), the authorized PD is the PD that administers governmental affairs in the field of protection of women and children as well as social affairs.

Article 22
